  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Lavani Marathi women's song-and-dance tradition of Maharashtra, characterized by powerful and often erotically suggestive female lead-singer-dancer performance accompanied by dholak two-headed barrel drum and tabla. Two main streams: nirguni lavani (philosophical-devotional) and shringari lavani (romantic-erotic, more popularly known). Performance traditionally occurs in folk-theatre tamasha contexts in nineteenth-and-twentieth-century rural Maharashtra, with the kalavantin dancer-singer holding a respected (if socially marginalized) professional role. Mid-twentieth-century Marathi-cinema adopted lavani as iconic regional cultural-form.",
